, which could be addressed.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 1's point and provide evidence from our notes. Provide explicit facts: B very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills; but makes nasty remarks. Compare with C's difficulty communicating and egocentric.\n\nThus we can argue that B's reliability and stress resilience are more critical than C's decision speed, and that C's communication issues are more severe (egocentric) than B's nasty remarks? Both are serious. But we can argue that B's conscientiousness indicates operational reliability, which is paramount.\n\nThus we can change recommendation to Candidate B.\n\nWe must produce public message: state recommendation, reference Agent 1's recommendation, give evidence, explain why we think B is better.\n\nLet's craft.\n\nMetadata vote: Candidate B."}
