ther to keep recommending Candidate C or switch to B. The current panel: Agent 1 originally recommended C, then Agent 2 and 3 switched to B, and Agent 2 reaffirmed B. Agent 3 also reaffirmed B. So currently 3 votes for B, 1 for C. As Agent 1, we can either maintain C or switch to B. The instruction says we can revise our recommendation based on combined evidence. We need to consider the evidence: we have explicit reliability for C (100% reliable) and for B (very conscientious). Both strong. B has weak memory for numbers (attention) and nasty remarks (crew cooperation). C has difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). Also C has excellent attention, calm, decision quality. B has good technical competence (weather, computer). Both have stress resilience.\n\nWe need to decide. The panel seems leaning B. As Agent 1, we could reconsider and maybe switch to B, providing reasoning that B's reliability and stress resilience outweigh C's communication issues, and that memory weakness can be mitigated. Or we could argue that C's reliability is absolute and his attention is excellent, making him better. But the other agents have already argued that B's reliability and stress are more critical, and that C's communication issues are deeper. We need to decide whether to change vote.\n\nGiven the panel majority, and the arguments that B's issues are more remediable, I think Agent 1 may switch to B. Provide reasoning referencing earlier points: C's communication difficulty and egocentric attitude may be more problematic than B's memory weakness, and B's reliability is strong. Also note that C's lack of willingness to further education is a concern for long-term development.\n\nThus, Agent 1 will now recommend Candidate B, citing explicit facts: B very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills; C difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education. Also note that B's weak memory for numbers is a concern but can be mitigated.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B."}
